# Frame windows 002-tilegrid cannot produce, one tile per line:
#   <tile> <baseaddr> <frames> <offset> <words>   (offset/words in halfwords)
# Applied by tools/fill_tilegrid_windows.py from env/finish_tilegrid.sh.
#
# CFG_CONFIG_X35Y120 (CONFIG_SITE: ICAP, STARTUP, BSCAN...). Frame column
# 0x6C sits between INT_INTF_R_PCIE4_X34 (0x6B) and INT_X35 (0x6E) and has 10
# minors in every row (counted in Vivado's own bitstreams). The tile spans its
# whole 60-row clock region (row field 2), so the window is the whole frame.
# designs/kv260_cfg_char icap vs base: Vivado's ICAPE3 sets 00_1892 01_1891
# 01_1892 here and nothing else in the column's row 2, and on the board an
# ICAPE3 reads all-zero without exactly those bits (kv260_icap_idcode).
CFG_CONFIG_X35Y120 0x00086C00 10 0 186

# CMT_L (MMCM, PLLs, BUFGCE/BUFGCTRL/BUFGCE_DIV). 002 found only the clock
# row (offset 84, 10 halfwords); the tile spans its 60-row region, and the
# column 0x33 has 12 minors in every row. designs/kv260_cmt_char: Vivado's
# MMCME4 at MMCM_X0Y0 sets halfwords 84-171 of the column's row 0, its PLLE4 at
# PLL_X0Y5 halfwords 42-83 of row 2, a BUFGCE 92-99. So the window is the whole
# frame; segbits_cmt_l.corrections counts from halfword 0 (2026-10-26).
CMT_L_X16Y0   0x00003300 12 0 186 widens
CMT_L_X16Y60  0x00043300 12 0 186 widens
CMT_L_X16Y120 0x00083300 12 0 186 widens
CMT_L_X16Y180 0x000C3300 12 0 186 widens
# RCLK_RCLK_XIPHY_INNER_FT: frame column 0x32 (4 minors), the clock row like
# every RCLK tile. MMCM, PLL and BUFGCE specimens all change 1518/1519/1532
# there (minors 2-3), and Vivado's PS-clock baseline sets 1518.
RCLK_RCLK_XIPHY_INNER_FT_X16Y29  0x00003200 4 93 3
RCLK_RCLK_XIPHY_INNER_FT_X16Y89  0x00043200 4 93 3
RCLK_RCLK_XIPHY_INNER_FT_X16Y149 0x00083200 4 93 3
RCLK_RCLK_XIPHY_INNER_FT_X16Y209 0x000C3200 4 93 3

# DSP (DSP48E2 x2), 2026-10-27, designs/kv260_dsp_char/gen_window.py: one
# DSP48E2 with default attributes at DSP48E2_X4Y0/X4Y1 (DSP_X12Y0), X4Y2
# (DSP_X12Y5), X4Y60 (DSP_X12Y150) and X0Y0 (DSP_X1Y0), each against a
# design without it. Every change outside INT/CLE windows lands in the frame
# column one above INT_X<n>'s (0x27 for X12, 0x05 for X1), which has 8 minors
# in every row, at INT_X<n>Y<y>'s halfword offset, spanning 15 halfwords (the
# tile's five INT rows): site 0 in the lower half, site 1 the upper. So
# DSP_X<n>Y<y> = INT_X<n>Y<y> column + 1, 8 frames, INT offset, 15 words.
DSP_X1Y0 0x00000500 8 0 15
DSP_X1Y5 0x00000500 8 15 15
DSP_X1Y10 0x00000500 8 30 15
DSP_X1Y15 0x00000500 8 45 15
DSP_X1Y20 0x00000500 8 60 15
